A||N||7||SKIDMARK||2.8 upgrade to 3.1||||5||
Z||000000||SKIDMARK||09-30-2001||07:48 AM||||What does it take to upgrade the stock 2.8 to a 3.1? I hear there are stroker kits available. Do these kits require boring the cylinders? Who has the best kit?<BR>I just want to upgrade my engine without changing the stock appearance. A few more hp<BR>without the expense of a swap. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||09-30-2001||08:29 AM||||Welcome to the forum.  There are kit to make a 3.1 but if you are going to all that trouble you could put in a 3.4  The 3.4 still allow you to put all the Fiero equipment on the engine so it will look completely stock.  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||dgroves||09-30-2001||04:14 PM||||Just putting mine back togather now. Much easier than I had origionally thought. Here's what you need. Crank from a 3.1. I bought a rebuilt one. It was the same price as a 2.8 but I had to pay a $20.00 core charge because I didn't have a 3.1 to turn back in. Next you will need a set of Silvolite #1486 pistons in whatever overbore you need. You use the 2.8 rods. The resulting compression ratio will be 8.8:1 I chose the Crane 2030 cam. it comes with a set of lifters. The only other mod is to remove the weight from the flywheel/flexplate. The 3.1 crank is balanced and dosen't need the counterweight. It all goes back toghther as you would assemble anything else. Mods are probably good for ~20 HP.||||reg||6
Z||000003||dgroves||09-30-2001||05:33 PM||||Hey.. I got a correction on that last post. I just went up to the garage to work on my car and discovered that the flexplate with the counterweight removed will not be neutural. I'll have to go to the junk yard and find a 3.1 flexplate. Suposedly in '88 GM went to neutural balance on all 60 degree v-6's. Shouldn't be too hard to find.<P>Sorry for the mis-info.||||reg||4
Z||000004||Shaun41178||09-30-2001||07:02 PM||||dgroves:  I have a neutral flexplate for a 3.1 crank.  I will sell it to you.  Its brand new.  Well from autozone anyways.  $20 +$5 for shipping and it is yours.  I think I payed $35 from Autozone.<P>If anyone would like a complete 3.1 rotating assembly I have one.  Brand new never used.  Crank is brand new.  Rods are all brand new.  Will come with a flexplate ad harmonic balancer.  You will need new pistons for iron heads though but if you are rebuilding then you will need new ones anyways.  Email me if you have any questions and for price.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gerald||10-02-2001||10:43 AM||||The stock 2.8 rods work????????<BR>Could somone please explain this to me. Wouldnt the pistons top out on the head because of the longer stroke? <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||10-02-2001||11:40 AM||||I believe the wrist pins are mounted higher in the pistons to allow you to use the 2.8 rods.<P>Keep in mind that you not only gain the horsepower but a pretty good increase in torque.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shaun41178||10-02-2001||04:01 PM||||the 3.1 rods are the same as the 2.8 rods.  same part number and everything.<P>only difference is crank and pistons and flexplate/flywheel.  <P>Check the archives and use the search function as this has all been discussed to death.  Everything you need to know is in past threads.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
